  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Business (BS). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] BUSN 403 is required for students admitted through change of major or transfer admissions process.\n[grid1 fn2] MATH 148 , MATH 152 , MATH 168 and MATH 172 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 140 .\n[grid1 fn3] MATH 147 , MATH 151 and MATH 171 will be accepted in lieu of MATH 142 .\n[grid1 fn4] For those students under ROTC contract, see Requirement 7 of the Requirements for a Baccalaureate Degree.\n[grid1 fn5] STAT 211 will be accepted in lieu of BUSN 203 .\n[grid1 fn6] Includes 12-18 hours of courses that were used to satisfy the required Minor or Certificate requirement and 9-15 hours of 100-499 courses not used elsewhere, except ACCT 209 , ACCT 210 , FINC 409 , IBUS 301 , ISTM 209 , MGMT 209 , MGMT 309 , MKTG 409 , SCMT 309 . Additional restrictions may apply; see academic advisor for information. May be taken on a satisfactory basis.\n[grid1 fn7] In consultation with advisor select from approved science and mathematics courses. Courses counting towards a certificate or minor may also fulfill these requirements.",
